  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m carefully dissecting the project\'s requirements. The key focus is a polished, interactive web application, \"E-Commerce Database Design & Normalization.\" I\'m noting the title, subtitle, and the need for a modern design. I see this as a Semester 3 individual project, which clarifies the scope somewhat, but I will need to clarify the interactive educational aspect.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Style**\n\nI\'ve been busy establishing the visual language. I\'m leaning toward a dark navy/charcoal base with blue/cyan accents. Purple will highlight normalization concepts, green will emphasize primary keys, orange will be for foreign keys, and red will signify dependencies. The plan is for rounded cards, subtle shadows, and a responsive layout with a collapsible mobile navigation. I\'m also planning the specific navigation items, and I\'m adding a global search bar. I\'m also outlining a presentation mode. I am debating 19 vs 21 entities.\n\n\n**Refining Entity Schema**\n\nI\'m now deep in the details of the database schema. I\'ve landed on a design with 19 core entities, not the previously considered 21, as I refined and consolidated them. I have the customer, contact, address, location, and product data finalized. I\'m focusing on attributes and keys, especially for the product catalog, which includes category, brand, and product itself.\n\n\n**Finalizing Table Relationships**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the database schema relationships, ensuring everything is properly linked. I\'ve defined the tables for orders, financials, items, payments, methods, statuses, and shipments. I\'ve also added the carriers and service levels. I\'m double-checking the foreign key constraints and the cardinality of all relationships to ensure data integrity and avoid redundancy.\n\n\n**Mapping Relationships Now**\n\nI\'m presently focusing on mapping the relationships between the database tables. I have finalized relationships between orders, payments, shipments, products, inventory, suppliers, payment methods, and statuses. Additionally, I\'ve defined relationships for shipments, carriers, service levels, categories, brands, and order items. I\'m focusing on the foreign key constraints and cardinality.\n\nI am developing an interactive ERD explorer. It will be an SVG canvas with zoom, pan, and draggable entity cards. Relationship lines will be interactive bezier or orthogonal lines with cardinality badges. Clicking an entity will select and highlight. The entity details drawer will open on click, with full schema. Clicking the relationship line will open a modal with relationship details.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Learning**\n\nI\'m now devising the interactive learning components. I\'ve mapped a step selector for the normalization journey, from overview through 3NF and a summary comparison. I\'m focusing on visual transformations for 1NF, 2NF, and 3NF, including before-and-after diff views and functional dependency diagrams. Specifically, I\'m thinking about a card browser showing the normalization of the original base tables and developing a Functional Dependency Explorer. I am also working on relationship details.\n\n\n**Developing Schema Browser**\n\nI am now developing a schema browser. I plan for a clean, tabular format and DDL code generation for all tables. I\'ll highlight primary keys in green and foreign keys in amber, making the references clear. Filters will be available by domain, and search by table/column.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m focused on the Data Explorer. I\'m building a simulated relational database with tabs for Customers, Products, Orders, and other entities. I\'m loading realistic sample records. I am implementing search, filter, pagination, and row selection. I am making it possible to inspect relational links (e.g., clicking an order to see its customer and items). Additionally, I have begun to build an SQL Playground with interactive SQL and preset queries.\n\n\n**Implementing SQL Playground**\n\nI\'m deep in the SQL playground now, writing the parser. I have the basic SELECT, FROM, JOIN (INNER), and WHERE clauses working with basic operators. ORDER BY, LIMIT, and error handling are next. I\'m building a query execution timer and a table result view. I have a plan for \"Clear,\" \"Run Query,\" \"Load Example,\" and \"Export CSV\" buttons. The plan is to create several realistic example queries. I\'m working on several queries: `SELECT ProductID, ProductName, Price FROM Products;`, `SELECT OrderID, Amount FROM Payments WHERE StatusID = 2;`, `SELECT OrderID, TotalAmount, Status FROM Orders JOIN OrderFinancials ON Orders.OrderID = OrderFinancials.OrderID;` and `SELECT TrackingNo, CarrierName, EstDeliveryDays FROM Shipments JOIN Carriers ON Shipments.CarrierID = Carriers.CarrierID JOIN ServiceLevels ON Shipments.ServiceLevelID = ServiceLevels.ServiceLevelID;`.\n\n\n\n**Structuring Project Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focused on project structure, planning a modular `src/` directory. I\'m finalizing data types in `database.ts`, and I\'ll include the complete data set for the 19 entities in `databaseData.ts`. I am creating a `sqlEngine.ts` to host my in-browser SQL parser. Also, I\'m designing key components: `Header.tsx`, `Sidebar.tsx`, `Overview.tsx`, and `ERDCanvas.tsx`. Full keyboard navigation, a fullscreen button, and a slide jumper are planned. Finally, I will write the Project Report.\n\n\n**Defining Component Breakdown**\n\nI\'m now detailing all interactive components and designing their individual roles. I am working on `EntityDrawer.tsx` for entity details and `RelationshipModal.tsx` for relationship inspection. There will also be a `EntitiesBrowser.tsx` for entity catalog and a `NormalizationLab.tsx` for normalization visualizations. I\'m also planning the `RelationalSchema.tsx` for schema viewing and SQL generation. I\'ll add the `DataExplorer.tsx` and `SQLPlayground.tsx` components. Then I will add the `DependencyExplorer.tsx` and a presentation mode.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_169147"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"export type DomainType = \\n  | \'Customer\' \\n  | \'Address\' \\n  | \'Product\' \\n  | \'Inventory\' \\n  | \'Orders\' \\n  | \'Payments\' \\n  | \'Shipping\' \\n  | \'Lookup\';\\n\\nexport type Cardinality = \'1:1\' | \'1:M\' | \'M:1\' | \'M:M\';\\n\\nexport interface Attribute {\\n  name: string;\\n  type: string;\\n  isPK?: boolean;\\n  isFK?: boolean;\\n  references?: string; // e.g. \\\"Customers.CustomerID\\\"\\n  nullable?: boolean;\\n  description?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Entity {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  domain: DomainType;\\n  purpose: string;\\n  isDocumentedExtra?: boolean; // For Inventory and Suppliers (part of 21-entity schema)\\n  isLookup?: boolean;\\n  attributes: Attribute[];\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Relationship {\\n  id: string;\\n  parent: string;\\n  child: string;\\n  cardinality: Cardinality;\\n  description: string;\\n  businessRule: string;\\n  parentKey: string;\\n  childKey: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface BaseTableTransformation {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  domain: DomainType;\\n  originalPurpose: string;\\n  originalColumns: string[];\\n  anomalies: string[];\\n  nf1Explanation: string;\\n  nf2Explanation: string;\\n  nf3Explanation: string;\\n  resultingEntities: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface FunctionalDependency {\\n  entityId: string;\\n  entityName: string;\\n  determinant: string;\\n  dependents: string[];\\n  transitiveDependencies?: {\\n    via: string;\\n    target: string;\\n    solution: string;\\n  }[];\\n  partialDependencies?: {\\n    compositeKey: string[];\\n    partialKey: string;\\n    dependent: string;\\n    solution: string;\\n  }[];\\n  normalFormAchieved: string;\\n}\\n\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/database.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating database types\", \"toolSummary\":\"Define TypeScript interfaces for database models\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "create_file"
    }
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 136412816
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "wI-7arG1CYrmvdIP4s-3mQg"
  }
