  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Data Entities**\n\nI\'ve outlined 21 key entities based on the report and schema documents. This includes 19 explicit final entities plus the Inventory and Suppliers schema entities. I\'ve also begun mapping relationships, starting with Customer-Order and Customer-Contact associations, which I am now fleshing out completely.\n\n\n**Mapping Relationships & Refining**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the relationships, specifically focusing on the connections between various entities. This includes detailed mappings like Customers to Customer Status (1:1), Customers to Customer Status History (1:M), Location to Address (1:1), and many more. I\'ve also identified key sample records and their potential representation within the database (e.g., Hira Raza, Samsung S24 Ultra, Leopard, etc.). Furthermore, I have defined nine base table transformations, along with the before/after states of the data and transformations. Finally, I defined functional dependencies for many key tables and created preset SQL queries.\n\nLet\'s create `src/data/databaseData.ts`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_114196"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"import { Entity, Relationship, BaseTableTransformation, FunctionalDependency } from \'../types/database\';\\n\\nexport const ENTITIES: Entity[] = [\\n  // 1. Customer & Contact\\n  {\\n    id: \'customers\',\\n    name: \'Customers\',\\n    domain: \'Customer\',\\n    purpose: \'Stores core customer master information separated from contact methods and lifecycle statuses.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'CustomerID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Surrogate primary key identifying the customer\' },\\n      { name: \'Name\', type: \'VARCHAR(100)\', description: \'Full legal name of the registered customer\' },\\n      { name: \'CreatedAt\', type: \'TIMESTAMP\', description: \'Account registration timestamp\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 60,\\n    y: 80,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'customer_contact\',\\n    name: \'Customer Contact\',\\n    domain: \'Customer\',\\n    purpose: \'Stores customer phone numbers and emails to eliminate repeating contact groups (1NF).\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'ContactID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Unique identifier for contact entry\' },\\n      { name: \'CustomerID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Customers.CustomerID\', description: \'Foreign key to parent customer\' },\\n      { name: \'Phone\', type: \'VARCHAR(25)\', description: \'Contact telephone number\' },\\n      { name: \'Email\', type: \'VARCHAR(120)\', description: \'Contact email address\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 60,\\n    y: 280,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'customer_status\',\\n    name: \'Customer Status\',\\n    domain: \'Customer\',\\n    isLookup: true,\\n    purpose: \'Maintains current operational lifecycle state of the customer account (3NF separation).\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'StatusID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary status key\' },\\n      { name: \'CustomerID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Customers.CustomerID\', description: \'Foreign key to customer\' },\\n      { name: \'Status\', type: \'VARCHAR(30)\', description: \'Current state: Active, Suspended, Inactive\' },\\n      { name: \'UpdatedAt\', type: \'TIMESTAMP\', description: \'Timestamp when status was updated\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 320,\\n    y: 80,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'customer_status_history\',\\n    name: \'Customer Status History\',\\n    domain: \'Customer\',\\n    purpose: \'Audit log capturing every historical status transition per customer.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'HistoryID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Unique historical log entry identifier\' },\\n      { name: \'CustomerID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Customers.CustomerID\', description: \'Foreign key to customer\' },\\n      { name: \'Status\', type: \'VARCHAR(30)\', description: \'Recorded status at transition\' },\\n      { name: \'ChangedAt\', type: \'TIMESTAMP\', description: \'Audit timestamp of the transition\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 320,\\n    y: 280,\\n  },\\n\\n  // 2. Address & Location\\n  {\\n    id: \'address\',\\n    name: \'Address\',\\n    domain: \'Address\',\\n    purpose: \'Physical postal address components normalized from location telemetry.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'AddressID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for address record\' },\\n      { name: \'Street\', type: \'VARCHAR(150)\', description: \'Physical street address lines\' },\\n      { name: \'City\', type: \'VARCHAR(80)\', description: \'City / Municipality\' },\\n      { name: \'PostalCode\', type: \'VARCHAR(20)\', description: \'Postal or ZIP code\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 60,\\n    y: 500,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'location\',\\n    name: \'Location\',\\n    domain: \'Address\',\\n    purpose: \'Geographic spatial coordinate mapping and zoning attributes.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'LocationID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Unique spatial location identifier\' },\\n      { name: \'AddressID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Address.AddressID\', description: \'Foreign key link to Address\' },\\n      { name: \'Latitude\', type: \'DECIMAL(9,6)\', description: \'GPS Latitude coordinate\' },\\n      { name: \'Longitude\', type: \'DECIMAL(9,6)\', description: \'GPS Longitude coordinate\' },\\n      { name: \'Zone\', type: \'VARCHAR(50)\', description: \'Logistics delivery hub or dispatch zone\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 320,\\n    y: 500,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'customer_address\',\\n    name: \'Customer Address\',\\n    domain: \'Address\',\\n    purpose: \'Associative entity resolving Many-to-Many linkage between Customers and Locations.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'CustomerAddressID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Unique identifier for mapping\' },\\n      { name: \'CustomerID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Customers.CustomerID\', description: \'Foreign key to Customer\' },\\n      { name: \'LocationID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Location.LocationID\', description: \'Foreign key to Location\' },\\n      { name: \'IsDefault\', type: \'BOOLEAN\', description: \'Whether this is primary delivery location\' },\\n      { name: \'AddressType\', type: \'VARCHAR(20)\', description: \'Billing, Shipping, or Office\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 180,\\n    y: 700,\\n  },\\n\\n  // 3. Product Catalog\\n  {\\n    id: \'category\',\\n    name: \'Category\',\\n    domain: \'Product\',\\n    isLookup: true,\\n    purpose: \'Hierarchical product classification extracted to remove 3NF transitive dependencies.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'CategoryID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for Category\' },\\n      { name: \'CategoryName\', type: \'VARCHAR(60)\', description: \'Display name: Smartphones, Laptops, etc.\' },\\n      { name: \'Description\', type: \'VARCHAR(200)\', nullable: true, description: \'Taxonomy classification details\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 600,\\n    y: 80,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'brand\',\\n    name: \'Brand\',\\n    domain: \'Product\',\\n    isLookup: true,\\n    purpose: \'Manufacturer and brand identity extracted to achieve 3NF.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'BrandID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for Brand\' },\\n      { name: \'BrandName\', type: \'VARCHAR(60)\', description: \'Brand name: Samsung, Apple, HP\' },\\n      { name: \'Country\', type: \'VARCHAR(60)\', nullable: true, description: \'Country of origin / HQ\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 850,\\n    y: 80,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'product\',\\n    name: \'Product\',\\n    domain: \'Product\',\\n    purpose: \'Core catalog item with foreign keys pointing to independent Brand and Category lookup tables.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'ProductID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for catalog item\' },\\n      { name: \'CategoryID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Category.CategoryID\', description: \'FK to Category\' },\\n      { name: \'BrandID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Brand.BrandID\', description: \'FK to Brand\' },\\n      { name: \'SKU\', type: \'VARCHAR(50)\', description: \'Stock Keeping Unit identifier\' },\\n      { name: \'ProductName\', type: \'VARCHAR(120)\', description: \'Commercial product title\' },\\n      { name: \'Price\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Retail selling price\' },\\n      { name: \'Cost\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Unit procurement acquisition cost\' },\\n      { name: \'Active\', type: \'BOOLEAN\', description: \'Catalog listing availability flag\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 720,\\n    y: 280,\\n  },\\n\\n  // 4. Inventory & Suppliers (Documented Entities)\\n  {\\n    id: \'inventory\',\\n    name: \'Inventory\',\\n    domain: \'Inventory\',\\n    isDocumentedExtra: true,\\n    purpose: \'Warehouse stock levels and reorder thresholds linked per product and procurement supplier.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'InventoryID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for warehouse stock line\' },\\n      { name: \'ProductID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Product.ProductID\', description: \'Foreign key to Product\' },\\n      { name: \'SupplierID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Suppliers.SupplierID\', description: \'Foreign key to supplying vendor\' },\\n      { name: \'Quantity\', type: \'INT\', description: \'Available stock on hand\' },\\n      { name: \'RestockLevel\', type: \'INT\', description: \'Safety threshold trigger for replenishment\' },\\n      { name: \'LastStocked\', type: \'DATE\', description: \'Date of most recent stock receipt\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 980,\\n    y: 450,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'suppliers\',\\n    name: \'Suppliers\',\\n    domain: \'Inventory\',\\n    isDocumentedExtra: true,\\n    purpose: \'Vendor directory detailing suppliers supplying products to the inventory warehouses.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'SupplierID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for Supplier\' },\\n      { name: \'SupplierName\', type: \'VARCHAR(100)\', description: \'Company or vendor trade name\' },\\n      { name: \'ContactName\', type: \'VARCHAR(80)\', description: \'Primary procurement representative\' },\\n      { name: \'Phone\', type: \'VARCHAR(30)\', description: \'Supplier direct hotline\' },\\n      { name: \'Email\', type: \'VARCHAR(100)\', description: \'Vendor corporate contact email\' },\\n      { name: \'City\', type: \'VARCHAR(60)\', description: \'Supplier operational headquarters\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 1220,\\n    y: 450,\\n  },\\n\\n  // 5. Orders\\n  {\\n    id: \'orders\',\\n    name: \'Orders\',\\n    domain: \'Orders\',\\n    purpose: \'Header transaction record representing a customer checkout session.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'OrderID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for sales order\' },\\n      { name: \'CustomerID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Customers.CustomerID\', description: \'Foreign key to ordering customer\' },\\n      { name: \'OrderDate\', type: \'TIMESTAMP\', description: \'Date and time of order checkout\' },\\n      { name: \'Status\', type: \'VARCHAR(30)\', description: \'Processing status: Placed, Confirmed, Shipped\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 520,\\n    y: 520,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'order_financials\',\\n    name: \'Order Financials\',\\n    domain: \'Orders\',\\n    purpose: \'One-to-One financial summary table tracking gross totals, taxes, and shipping fees.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'FinancialID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for ledger record\' },\\n      { name: \'OrderID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Orders.OrderID\', description: \'1:1 Foreign key to Order\' },\\n      { name: \'Subtotal\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Itemized items sum before tax and shipping\' },\\n      { name: \'TaxAmount\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Calculated value-added or sales tax\' },\\n      { name: \'ShippingFee\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Assessed logistics delivery fee\' },\\n      { name: \'TotalAmount\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Final payable order invoice total\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 760,\\n    y: 520,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'order_items\',\\n    name: \'Order Items\',\\n    domain: \'Orders\',\\n    purpose: \'Itemized line-item breakdown eliminating repeating order groups (1NF) & partial keys (2NF).\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'OrderItemID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Surrogate primary key for line item\' },\\n      { name: \'OrderID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Orders.OrderID\', description: \'Foreign key to parent Order\' },\\n      { name: \'ProductID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Product.ProductID\', description: \'Foreign key to catalog item\' },\\n      { name: \'Quantity\', type: \'INT\', description: \'Number of units ordered\' },\\n      { name: \'UnitPrice\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Price locked at time of purchase\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 640,\\n    y: 720,\\n  },\\n\\n  // 6. Payments\\n  {\\n    id: \'payments\',\\n    name: \'Payments\',\\n    domain: \'Payments\',\\n    purpose: \'Settlement transaction records associated with customer sales orders.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'PaymentID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for payment attempt\' },\\n      { name: \'OrderID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Orders.OrderID\', description: \'Foreign key to associated order\' },\\n      { name: \'MethodID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Payment Method.MethodID\', description: \'FK to payment method lookup\' },\\n      { name: \'StatusID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Payment Status.StatusID\', description: \'FK to payment status lookup\' },\\n      { name: \'Amount\', type: \'DECIMAL(10,2)\', description: \'Monetary settlement transaction amount\' },\\n      { name: \'GatewayRef\', type: \'VARCHAR(80)\', description: \'Payment gateway transaction trace ID\' },\\n      { name: \'AuthCode\', type: \'VARCHAR(40)\', description: \'Authorization verification code\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 480,\\n    y: 940,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'payment_method\',\\n    name: \'Payment Method\',\\n    domain: \'Payments\',\\n    isLookup: true,\\n    purpose: \'Lookup reference table for tender types: Card, COD, Wallet, etc.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'MethodID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for tender method\' },\\n      { name: \'MethodName\', type: \'VARCHAR(40)\', description: \'Card, COD, Mobile Wallet, Bank Transfer\' },\\n      { name: \'Description\', type: \'VARCHAR(150)\', nullable: true, description: \'Processing channel details\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 220,\\n    y: 940,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'payment_status\',\\n    name: \'Payment Status\',\\n    domain: \'Payments\',\\n    isLookup: true,\\n    purpose: \'Lookup reference table for payment lifecycle states: Pending, Captured, Refunded, Failed.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'StatusID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for status code\' },\\n      { name: \'StatusName\', type: \'VARCHAR(40)\', description: \'Pending, Captured, Voided, Failed\' },\\n      { name: \'Description\', type: \'VARCHAR(150)\', nullable: true, description: \'Lifecycle state rules\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 220,\\n    y: 1120,\\n  },\\n\\n  // 7. Shipping & Logistics\\n  {\\n    id: \'shipments\',\\n    name: \'Shipments\',\\n    domain: \'Shipping\',\\n    purpose: \'Fulfillment consignment tracking orders dispatched through third-party carriers.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'ShipmentID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for consignment shipment\' },\\n      { name: \'OrderID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Orders.OrderID\', description: \'Foreign key to parent order\' },\\n      { name: \'CarrierID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Carriers.CarrierID\', description: \'Foreign key to logistics carrier\' },\\n      { name: \'ServiceLevelID\', type: \'INT\', isFK: true, references: \'Service Levels.ServiceLevelID\', description: \'Foreign key to delivery tier\' },\\n      { name: \'TrackingNo\', type: \'VARCHAR(80)\', description: \'Courier waybill / tracking code\' },\\n      { name: \'ShipDate\', type: \'DATE\', description: \'Date dispatched from warehouse\' },\\n      { name: \'DeliveryDate\', type: \'DATE\', nullable: true, description: \'Date of final handover to recipient\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 940,\\n    y: 940,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'carriers\',\\n    name: \'Carriers\',\\n    domain: \'Shipping\',\\n    isLookup: true,\\n    purpose: \'Courier companies authorized for delivery: Leopard, BlueEx, TCS, etc.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'CarrierID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for logistics partner\' },\\n      { name: \'CarrierName\', type: \'VARCHAR(80)\', description: \'Leopard, BlueEx, TCS\' },\\n      { name: \'ContactPhone\', type: \'VARCHAR(30)\', description: \'Dispatch dispatch desk phone\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 1220,\\n    y: 940,\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'service_levels\',\\n    name: \'Service Levels\',\\n    domain: \'Shipping\',\\n    isLookup: true,\\n    purpose: \'Shipping speed tiers: Standard Delivery, Express Same-Day, Overnight.\',\\n    attributes: [\\n      { name: \'ServiceLevelID\', type: \'INT\', isPK: true, description: \'Primary key for SLA tier\' },\\n      { name: \'LevelName\', type: \'VARCHAR(50)\', description: \'Standard, Express, Overnight\' },\\n      { name: \'EstDeliveryDays\', type: \'INT\', description: \'Expected transit duration in business days\' },\\n    ],\\n    x: 1220,\\n    y: 1120,\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport const RELATIONSHIPS: Relationship[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_cust_orders\',\\n    parent: \'Customers\',\\n    child: \'Orders\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A customer can place multiple orders over time.\',\\n    businessRule: \'An order must be associated with exactly one customer; a registered customer can have zero or multiple orders.\',\\n    parentKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n    childKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_cust_contact\',\\n    parent: \'Customers\',\\n    child: \'Customer Contact\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A customer can have multiple contact channels (personal phone, business email).\',\\n    businessRule: \'Separated from Customers table to eliminate repeating phone/email columns (1NF atomic requirement).\',\\n    parentKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n    childKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_cust_status\',\\n    parent: \'Customers\',\\n    child: \'Customer Status\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:1\',\\n    description: \'A customer has exactly one active operational account status record.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Keeps current operational state clean and separated from immutable customer identity.\',\\n    parentKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n    childKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_cust_history\',\\n    parent: \'Customers\',\\n    child: \'Customer Status History\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'Historical audit log entries per customer transition.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Captures full timestamped audit trail of status changes (e.g., Pending -> Active -> Suspended).\',\\n    parentKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n    childKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_loc_addr\',\\n    parent: \'Location\',\\n    child: \'Address\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:1\',\\n    description: \'A geographic location maps directly to a physical postal address.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Decouples spatial GIS coordinate telemetry (lat/long/zone) from textual postal addresses.\',\\n    parentKey: \'AddressID\',\\n    childKey: \'AddressID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_loc_cust_addr\',\\n    parent: \'Location\',\\n    child: \'Customer Address\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A location can be linked to multiple customer address profiles.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Enables multiple customers residing in the same complex or building to share normalized location nodes.\',\\n    parentKey: \'LocationID\',\\n    childKey: \'LocationID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_cust_cust_addr\',\\n    parent: \'Customers\',\\n    child: \'Customer Address\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A customer can save multiple delivery addresses.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Customer can store Home, Work, and Billing addresses with one designated as default.\',\\n    parentKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n    childKey: \'CustomerID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_cat_prod\',\\n    parent: \'Category\',\\n    child: \'Product\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A product category contains multiple products.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Category name and description are normalized into Category table to eliminate 3NF transitive dependency.\',\\n    parentKey: \'CategoryID\',\\n    childKey: \'CategoryID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_brand_prod\',\\n    parent: \'Brand\',\\n    child: \'Product\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A brand manufactures multiple catalog products.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Brand metadata is segregated to prevent update anomalies across hundreds of SKUs.\',\\n    parentKey: \'BrandID\',\\n    childKey: \'BrandID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_orders_items\',\\n    parent: \'Orders\',\\n    child: \'Order Items\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'An order contains multiple itemized lines.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Removes repeating product columns from Orders (1NF) and resolves composite key partial dependencies (2NF).\',\\n    parentKey: \'OrderID\',\\n    childKey: \'OrderID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_prod_items\',\\n    parent: \'Product\',\\n    child: \'Order Items\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A product can be purchased across many order line items.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Connects sales demand to catalog items; unit price is snapshotted to preserve historical transaction integrity.\',\\n    parentKey: \'ProductID\',\\n    childKey: \'ProductID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_orders_fin\',\\n    parent: \'Orders\',\\n    child: \'Order Financials\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:1\',\\n    description: \'One financial summary ledger record per sales order.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Separates mutable order fulfillment status from immutable financial ledger calculations.\',\\n    parentKey: \'OrderID\',\\n    childKey: \'OrderID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_orders_pay\',\\n    parent: \'Orders\',\\n    child: \'Payments\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'Multiple payments or payment attempts may apply to an order.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Supports split payments, failed authorization retries, and partial refund settlements.\',\\n    parentKey: \'OrderID\',\\n    childKey: \'OrderID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_orders_ship\',\\n    parent: \'Orders\',\\n    child: \'Shipments\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'An order can generate multiple split shipments.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Accounts for warehouse dispatch from different geographic fulfillment facilities.\',\\n    parentKey: \'OrderID\',\\n    childKey: \'OrderID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_prod_inv\',\\n    parent: \'Product\',\\n    child: \'Inventory\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'A catalog product may appear in multiple inventory records across fulfillment centers.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Enables multi-warehouse tracking and safety stock replenishments.\',\\n    parentKey: \'ProductID\',\\n    childKey: \'ProductID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_inv_supp\',\\n    parent: \'Suppliers\',\\n    child: \'Inventory\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'Each supplier provides replenishment for multiple inventory lines.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Normalizes procurement vendor contact data and prevents supplier info redundancy.\',\\n    parentKey: \'SupplierID\',\\n    childKey: \'SupplierID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_pay_method\',\\n    parent: \'Payment Method\',\\n    child: \'Payments\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'Each payment uses one verified payment method.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Lookup table restricts payment methods to approved channels (Card, COD, Mobile Wallet).\',\\n    parentKey: \'MethodID\',\\n    childKey: \'MethodID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_pay_status\',\\n    parent: \'Payment Status\',\\n    child: \'Payments\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'Each payment transaction holds one current status code.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Lookup table standardizes settlement states (Pending, Captured, Failed).\',\\n    parentKey: \'StatusID\',\\n    childKey: \'StatusID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_ship_carrier\',\\n    parent: \'Carriers\',\\n    child: \'Shipments\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'Each consignment shipment uses one logistics carrier.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Third-party delivery partners (Leopard, BlueEx, TCS) managed via master carrier lookup.\',\\n    parentKey: \'CarrierID\',\\n    childKey: \'CarrierID\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'rel_ship_sla\',\\n    parent: \'Service Levels\',\\n    child: \'Shipments\',\\n    cardinality: \'1:M\',\\n    description: \'Each shipment operates under a designated service level SLA.\',\\n    businessRule: \'Defines delivery velocity expectations (Standard 3-5 days, Express 1-2 days).\',\\n    parentKey: \'ServiceLevelID\',\\n    childKey: \'ServiceLevelID\',\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport const BASE_TABLES: BaseTableTransformation[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_customers\',\\n    name: \'1. Customers (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Customer\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Monolithic table originally housing customer credentials, multiple telephone numbers, alternate emails, and account status transitions.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'CustomerID\', \'Name\', \'Phone1\', \'Phone2\', \'Email1\', \'Email2\', \'Status\', \'StatusChangedAt\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Repeating groups of contact methods (Phone1, Phone2, Email1, Email2) violating 1NF.\',\\n      \'Inability to record more than 2 numbers without schema alteration (DDL alteration penalty).\',\\n      \'Loss of status transition audit trail when overwriting Status field.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Extracted contact methods into a dedicated `Customer Contact` entity, converting repeating columns into atomic rows linked by CustomerID.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'CustomerID was already a single-attribute key, hence no partial functional dependency existed.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Separated mutable current status into `Customer Status` and historical audit logs into `Customer Status History`.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Customers\', \'Customer Contact\', \'Customer Status\', \'Customer Status History\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_address\',\\n    name: \'2. Address & Location (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Address\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Combined physical street address, geographical GPS latitude/longitude, delivery zoning, and customer delivery preferences.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'AddressID\', \'CustomerID\', \'Street\', \'City\', \'PostalCode\', \'Latitude\', \'Longitude\', \'Zone\', \'IsDefault\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Spatial coordinate telemetry mixed with postal address details.\',\\n      \'Redundant storage of identical addresses when multiple family members or office workers register.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Decomposed composite geographic descriptors into atomic data types.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'Removed direct dependency on CustomerID to allow shared locations and multiple delivery locations.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Split physical street/postal details into `Address`, spatial telemetry into `Location`, and resolved M:N relation via `Customer Address`.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Address\', \'Location\', \'Customer Address\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_products\',\\n    name: \'3. Products Catalog (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Product\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Single large catalog record storing item details, manufacturer brand attributes, and category classification in one place.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'ProductID\', \'ProductName\', \'SKU\', \'Price\', \'Cost\', \'CategoryID\', \'CategoryName\', \'BrandID\', \'BrandName\', \'BrandCountry\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Severe Transitive Dependency: ProductID -> CategoryID -> CategoryName.\',\\n      \'Severe Transitive Dependency: ProductID -> BrandID -> BrandName, BrandCountry.\',\\n      \'Update anomaly: Changing a brand name required updating thousands of product records.\',\\n      \'Deletion anomaly: Deleting the last product of a brand deleted the brand entirely.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Ensured atomic price, cost, SKU, and product name attributes.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'ProductID is a single primary key; all non-key attributes fully depend on ProductID.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Removed transitive dependencies by extracting `Category` and `Brand` into separate lookup entities, leaving foreign keys in `Product`.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Product\', \'Category\', \'Brand\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_inventory\',\\n    name: \'4. Inventory (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Inventory\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Stock management table storing warehouse quantities, supplier names, contact phone numbers, and procurement addresses.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'InventoryID\', \'ProductID\', \'Quantity\', \'SupplierID\', \'SupplierName\', \'SupplierPhone\', \'SupplierCity\', \'RestockLevel\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Transitive dependency: InventoryID -> SupplierID -> SupplierName, SupplierPhone, SupplierCity.\',\\n      \'Insertion anomaly: Inability to register a new vendor until an inventory item is created.\',\\n      \'Redundancy: Supplier contact details duplicated across dozens of stocked SKUs.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Atomic storage of integer quantities, reorder thresholds, and dates.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'Inventory records identified by surrogate InventoryID key.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Extracted vendor master data into `Suppliers`, retaining `SupplierID` as an FK in `Inventory`.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Inventory\', \'Suppliers\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_suppliers\',\\n    name: \'5. Suppliers (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Inventory\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Vendor procurement directory originally containing mixed supplier contracts and multiple supply warehouse links.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'SupplierID\', \'SupplierName\', \'ContactName\', \'Phone\', \'Email\', \'City\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Potential repeating contact numbers and untracked warehouse links.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Structured into atomic contact records.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'Key dependency intact; full functional dependency on SupplierID.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Standardized as an independent master entity referenced by Inventory.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Suppliers\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_orders\',\\n    name: \'6. Orders (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Orders\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Order header containing repeating items (Item1, Item2, Item3), prices, subtotals, tax rates, shipping fees, and payment notes.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'OrderID\', \'CustomerID\', \'OrderDate\', \'Item1_SKU\', \'Item1_Qty\', \'Item2_SKU\', \'Item2_Qty\', \'Subtotal\', \'Tax\', \'ShippingFee\', \'Total\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Massive 1NF violation: Repeating columns (Item1_SKU, Item1_Qty, Item2_SKU, Item2_Qty).\',\\n      \'Artificial limit on max items per order (cannot order 5 items if only 2 slots exist).\',\\n      \'Calculated totals mixed with core lifecycle timestamps.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Removed repeating item columns and created `Order Items` line items.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'Eliminated partial dependencies where item attributes depended only on product rather than the composite order context.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Isolated calculated monetary sums into a dedicated `Order Financials` 1:1 ledger.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Orders\', \'Order Items\', \'Order Financials\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_order_items\',\\n    name: \'7. Order Items (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Orders\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Line item records initially keyed with composite key (OrderID, ProductID) that also stored product descriptions and current catalog prices.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'OrderID\', \'ProductID\', \'ProductName\', \'ProductPrice\', \'Quantity\', \'LineTotal\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'2NF Violation: ProductName and ProductPrice depended only on ProductID (partial key), NOT on OrderID.\',\\n      \'If catalog price updated later, historical order lines erroneously recalculated.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Atomic quantities and snapshotted UnitPrice at time of checkout.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'Removed partial key dependency by delegating ProductName to catalog `Product` table and locking `UnitPrice` inside `Order Items`.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Removed calculated `LineTotal` (Quantity * UnitPrice) to eliminate transitive calculation dependency.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Order Items\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_payments\',\\n    name: \'8. Payments (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Payments\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Transaction table storing free-text payment method names, status strings, gateway responses, and authorization codes.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'PaymentID\', \'OrderID\', \'Amount\', \'PaymentMethod\', \'MethodFee\', \'PaymentStatus\', \'StatusRules\', \'GatewayRef\', \'AuthCode\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Inconsistent text entry for methods (\\\"CC\\\", \\\"Credit Card\\\", \\\"Visa\\\", \\\"Card\\\").\',\\n      \'Transitive dependency: PaymentID -> PaymentMethod -> MethodFee.\',\\n      \'Transitive dependency: PaymentID -> PaymentStatus -> StatusRules.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Structured transaction reference IDs and currency values.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'PaymentID is surrogate key; all attributes depend on PaymentID.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Extracted `Payment Method` and `Payment Status` into standard lookup reference tables.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Payments\', \'Payment Method\', \'Payment Status\'],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: \'base_shipments\',\\n    name: \'9. Shipments (Base)\',\\n    domain: \'Shipping\',\\n    originalPurpose: \'Logistics fulfillment records storing courier company names, phone numbers, delivery SLA descriptions, and transit dates.\',\\n    originalColumns: [\'ShipmentID\', \'OrderID\', \'CarrierName\', \'CarrierPhone\', \'ServiceLevel\', \'EstDays\', \'TrackingNo\', \'ShipDate\', \'DeliveryDate\'],\\n    anomalies: [\\n      \'Transitive dependency: ShipmentID -> CarrierName -> CarrierPhone.\',\\n      \'Transitive dependency: ShipmentID -> ServiceLevel -> EstDays.\',\\n      \'Carrier contact updates required mass updates across all historical shipments.\',\\n    ],\\n    nf1Explanation: \'Standardized tracking waybills and calendar dispatch dates.\',\\n    nf2Explanation: \'All non-key shipment attributes depend on ShipmentID.\',\\n    nf3Explanation: \'Extracted courier data into `Carriers` and transit SLA terms into `Service Levels`.\',\\n    resultingEntities: [\'Shipments\', \'Carriers\', \'Service Levels\'],\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport const FUNCTIONAL_DEPENDENCIES: FunctionalDependency[] = [\\n  {\\n    entityId: \'product\',\\n    entityName: \'Product (Catalog)\',\\n    determinant: \'ProductID\',\\n    dependents: [\'SKU\', \'ProductName\', \'Price\', \'Cost\', \'Active\', \'CategoryID\', \'BrandID\'],\\n    transitiveDependencies: [\\n      {\\n        via: \'CategoryID\',\\n        target: \'CategoryName, Description\',\\n        solution: \'Normalized into separate Category table (CategoryID -> CategoryName). Resolved to 3NF.\',\\n      },\\n      {\\n        via: \'BrandID\',\\n        target: \'BrandName, Country\',\\n        solution: \'Normalized into separate Brand table (BrandID -> BrandName). Resolved to 3NF.\',\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    normalFormAchieved: \'3NF (Third Normal Form)\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    entityId: \'order_items\',\\n    entityName: \'Order Items (Sales)\',\\n    determinant: \'OrderItemID (or composite {OrderID, ProductID})\',\\n    dependents: [\'OrderID\', \'ProductID\', \'Quantity\', \'UnitPrice\'],\\n    partialDependencies: [\\n      {\\n        compositeKey: [\'OrderID\', \'ProductID\'],\\n        partialKey: \'ProductID\',\\n        dependent: \'ProductName, ProductCost\',\\n        solution: \'ProductName depends only on ProductID. Moved ProductName out to Product table, keeping only ProductID and transaction UnitPrice.\',\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    normalFormAchieved: \'3NF / BCNF\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    entityId: \'orders\',\\n    entityName: \'Orders (Transaction Header)\',\\n    determinant: \'OrderID\',\\n    dependents: [\'CustomerID\', \'OrderDate\', \'Status\'],\\n    transitiveDependencies: [\\n      {\\n        via: \'CustomerID\',\\n        target: \'CustomerName, Phone, Email\',\\n        solution: \'Customer contact attributes depend on CustomerID, not OrderID. Separated into Customers table.\',\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    normalFormAchieved: \'3NF\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    entityId: \'payments\',\\n    entityName: \'Payments (Settlement)\',\\n    determinant: \'PaymentID\',\\n    dependents: [\'OrderID\', \'MethodID\', \'StatusID\', \'Amount\', \'GatewayRef\', \'AuthCode\'],\\n    transitiveDependencies: [\\n      {\\n        via: \'MethodID\',\\n        target: \'MethodName, MethodDescription\',\\n        solution: \'Method metadata depends on MethodID. Normalized into Payment Method lookup.\',\\n      },\\n      {\\n        via: \'StatusID\',\\n        target: \'StatusName, StatusDescription\',\\n        solution: \'Status metadata depends on StatusID. Normalized into Payment Status lookup.\',\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    normalFormAchieved: \'3NF\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    entityId: \'shipments\',\\n    entityName: \'Shipments (Fulfillment)\',\\n    determinant: \'ShipmentID\',\\n    dependents: [\'OrderID\', \'CarrierID\', \'ServiceLevelID\', \'TrackingNo\', \'ShipDate\', \'DeliveryDate\'],\\n    transitiveDependencies: [\\n      {\\n        via: \'CarrierID\',\\n        target: \'CarrierName, ContactPhone\',\\n        solution: \'Courier details depend on CarrierID. Separated into Carriers table.\',\\n      },\\n      {\\n        via: \'ServiceLevelID\',\\n        target: \'LevelName, EstDeliveryDays\',\\n        solution: \'SLA parameters depend on ServiceLevelID. Separated into Service Levels table.\',\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    normalFormAchieved: \'3NF\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    entityId: \'customers\',\\n    entityName: \'Customers (Master)\',\\n    determinant: \'CustomerID\',\\n    dependents: [\'Name\', \'CreatedAt\'],\\n    transitiveDependencies: [\\n      {\\n        via: \'StatusID\',\\n        target: \'StatusName, UpdatedAt\',\\n        solution: \'Status lifecycle decoupled into Customer Status and Customer Status History.\',\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    normalFormAchieved: \'3NF\',\\n  },\\n];\\n\\n// Sample data exactly grounded in the student project report\\nexport const SAMPLE_DATA: Record<string, Record<string, unknown>[]> = {\\n  Customers: [\\n    { CustomerID: 1, Name: \'Hira Raza\', CreatedAt: \'2024-11-12 10:15:00\' },\\n    { CustomerID: 2, Name: \'Usman Yousaf\', CreatedAt: \'2024-10-14 14:30:00\' },\\n    { CustomerID: 3, Name: \'Hira Yousaf\', CreatedAt: \'2025-06-14 09:20:00\' },\\n    { CustomerID: 4, Name: \'Bilal Ahmed\', CreatedAt: \'2025-07-01 11:45:00\' },\\n    { CustomerID: 5, Name: \'Ayesha Khan\', CreatedAt: \'2025-08-19 16:10:00\' },\\n  ],\\n  \'Customer Contact\': [\\n    { ContactID: 1, CustomerID: 1, Phone: \'+92 321 2188789\', Email: \'hira.raza@gmail.com\' },\\n    { ContactID: 2, CustomerID: 2, Phone: \'+92 334 3219824\', Email: \'usmanyousaf@gmail.com\' },\\n    { ContactID: 3, CustomerID: 3, Phone: \'+92 312 2582524\', Email: \'hira.yousaf@retail.pk\' },\\n    { ContactID: 4, CustomerID: 4, Phone: \'+92 300 4589123\', Email: \'bilal.ahmed@cloud.com\' },\\n    { ContactID: 5, CustomerID: 5, Phone: \'+92 345 8891204\', Email: \'ayesha.k@matrix.org\' },\\n  ],\\n  \'Customer Status\': [\\n    { StatusID: 1, CustomerID: 1, Status: \'Active\', UpdatedAt: \'2024-11-12 10:15:00\' },\\n    { StatusID: 2, CustomerID: 2, Status: \'Active\', UpdatedAt: \'2024-10-14 14:30:00\' },\\n    { StatusID: 3, CustomerID: 3, Status: \'Active\', UpdatedAt: \'2025-06-14 09:20:00\' },\\n    { StatusID: 4, CustomerID: 4, Status: \'Suspended\', UpdatedAt: \'2025-08-01 12:00:00\' },\\n    { StatusID: 5, CustomerI