    started_at {
      seconds: 1790677267
      nanos: 159368179
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    response: "An interactive educational web application titled **E-Commerce Database Design & Normalization** has been built for the **Database Systems (Semester 3)** individual project by **Muhammad Abu Bakar (FA24-BBD-109)**, prepared for **Sir Ayyaz Mahmood**.\n\n### Highlights of the Implementation\n\n1. **Interactive ERD Explorer Canvas**\n   - **Vector Graphic Topology**: Draggable entity cards rendered on an interactive grid canvas with smooth pan, wheel zoom, zoom controls (`Zoom +`, `Zoom -`, `Fit`, `Reset`), and domain filtering.\n   - **Visual Key Hierarchy**: Emerald green for Primary Keys (`PK`), amber orange for Foreign Keys (`FK`), blue for attributes, and purple for lookup tables.\n   - **Interactive Relationship Highlighting**: Selecting an entity (e.g., `Orders`) highlights all referentially connected entities (`Customers`, `Order Items`, `Order Financials`, `Payments`, `Shipments`) while dimming unrelated nodes, accompanied by an interactive connection tree.\n   - **Clickable Relationship Lines & Entity Drawer**: Clicking any connection line displays its business rule, cardinality (`1:1`, `1:M`, `M:1`), and parent/child constraints in a detailed modal. Clicking an entity opens a slide-over drawer with column schemas, referential paths, and report-grounded sample rows.\n\n2. **19 vs. 21 Entity Academic Consistency Toggle**\n   - Transparently handles the report\'s numerical variations with a live toggle:\n     - **19 Final Entities**: The authoritative explicit list from the report summary.\n     - **21 Complete Documented Entities**: Incorporates documented `Inventory` and `Suppliers` entities into the active schema, updating all metrics and relationships dynamically.\n\n3. **Normalization Lab (1NF \342\206\222 2NF \342\206\222 3NF) & 9 Base Tables Explorer**\n   - **1NF Lab**: Visual before/after comparison contrasting unnormalized repeating groups (`Product1`, `Qty1`, `Product2`, `Qty2`) with atomic `Orders` and `Order Items` decomposition.\n   - **2NF Dependency Graph**: Explains composite key dependencies on `{OrderID, ProductID}` and how partial dependencies (`ProductName`) are segregated to the catalog `Product` entity.\n   - **3NF Transitive Dependency Visualizer**: Interactive chains (`ProductID \342\206\222 CategoryID \342\206\222 CategoryName` and `ProductID \342\206\222 BrandID \342\206\222 BrandName`) showcasing how lookup entities prevent update and deletion anomalies.\n   - **9 Base Tables Explorer**: Dedicated card inspector for all 9 foundational tables detailing their original schema, anomalies, and multi-stage normalization outcomes.\n\n4. **In-Browser SQL Playground**\n   - Client-side SQL execution engine supporting `SELECT`, `FROM`, `INNER JOIN`, `WHERE` (arithmetic and string comparisons, `AND`/`OR`), `ORDER BY`, and `LIMIT`.\n   - Pre-configured showcase queries, query execution timer (in milliseconds), row counter, CSV result export, and detailed syntax/table validation.\n\n5. **Live Data Explorer & Relational Schema Browser**\n   - Realistic sample records matching the report (`Hira Raza`, `Usman Yousaf`, `Samsung S24 Ultra`, `iPhone 15 Pro Max`, `HP Victus 15`, `Leopard`, `BlueEx`, `TCS`, etc.).\n   - Full SQL `CREATE TABLE` DDL generator with one-click clipboard copying.\n\n6. **Presentation Viva Mode & Global Search**\n   - **Presentation Mode**: Fullscreen, keyboard-navigable (`\342\206\220` / `\342\206\222` / `Space`) 9-slide defense deck structured for academic evaluation.\n   - **Global Search (`\342\214\230K` / `Ctrl+K`)**: Rapidly searches and cross-references entities, individual table attributes (e.g., typing `CustomerID` lists all parent and child tables), and relationship rules."
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Parameters**\n\nOkay, I\'m now cross-referencing all details from the initial request to confirm every parameter is correctly understood. I am verifying the project title, subtitle, student details, and instructor information against the user\'s initial requirements. Ensuring everything aligns now will save considerable time later in development.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Framework**\n\nI\'ve been solidifying the visual framework. The design is leaning towards a dark navy/charcoal primary theme, with blue and cyan accents. Purple is slated for normalization, green for primary keys, orange for foreign keys, and red for warnings. I\'m aiming for rounded cards and a responsive mobile layout with a left sidebar featuring nine navigation items.\n\n\n**Outlining Database Diagrams**\n\nI\'m now detailing the database diagrams. The goal is a drawer showing entity details, including name, purpose, primary and foreign keys, attributes with data types, and relationships with cardinality. I\'m also planning a complete relationship dataset with business rules and descriptions and an entity browser with search and filtering features. Normalization visualizations are in progress too.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "An interactive educational web application titled **E-Commerce Database Design & Normalization** has been built for the **Database Systems (Semester 3)** individual project by **Muhammad Abu Bakar (FA24-BBD-109)**, prepared for **Sir Ayyaz Mahmood**.\n\n### Highlights of the Implementation\n\n1. **Interactive ERD Explorer Canvas**\n   - **Vector Graphic Topology**: Draggable entity cards rendered on an interactive grid canvas with smooth pan, wheel zoom, zoom controls (`Zoom +`, `Zoom -`, `Fit`, `Reset`), and domain filtering.\n   - **Visual Key Hierarchy**: Emerald green for Primary Keys (`PK`), amber orange for Foreign Keys (`FK`), blue for attributes, and purple for lookup tables.\n   - **Interactive Relationship Highlighting**: Selecting an entity (e.g., `Orders`) highlights all referentially connected entities (`Customers`, `Order Items`, `Order Financials`, `Payments`, `Shipments`) while dimming unrelated nodes, accompanied by an interactive connection tree.\n   - **Clickable Relationship Lines & Entity Drawer**: Clicking any connection line displays its business rule, cardinality (`1:1`, `1:M`, `M:1`), and parent/child constraints in a detailed modal. Clicking an entity opens a slide-over drawer with column schemas, referential paths, and report-grounded sample rows.\n\n2. **19 vs. 21 Entity Academic Consistency Toggle**\n   - Transparently handles the report\'s numerical variations with a live toggle:\n     - **19 Final Entities**: The authoritative explicit list from the report summary.\n     - **21 Complete Documented Entities**: Incorporates documented `Inventory` and `Suppliers` entities into the active schema, updating all metrics and relationships dynamically.\n\n3. **Normalization Lab (1NF \342\206\222 2NF \342\206\222 3NF) & 9 Base Tables Explorer**\n   - **1NF Lab**: Visual before/after comparison contrasting unnormalized repeating groups (`Product1`, `Qty1`, `Product2`, `Qty2`) with atomic `Orders` and `Order Items` decomposition.\n   - **2NF Dependency Graph**: Explains composite key dependencies on `{OrderID, ProductID}` and how partial dependencies (`ProductName`) are segregated to the catalog `Product` entity.\n   - **3NF Transitive Dependency Visualizer**: Interactive chains (`ProductID \342\206\222 CategoryID \342\206\222 CategoryName` and `ProductID \342\206\222 BrandID \342\206\222 BrandName`) showcasing how lookup entities prevent update and deletion anomalies.\n   - **9 Base Tables Explorer**: Dedicated card inspector for all 9 foundational tables detailing their original schema, anomalies, and multi-stage normalization outcomes.\n\n4. **In-Browser SQL Playground**\n   - Client-side SQL execution engine supporting `SELECT`, `FROM`, `INNER JOIN`, `WHERE` (arithmetic and string comparisons, `AND`/`OR`), `ORDER BY`, and `LIMIT`.\n   - Pre-configured showcase queries, query execution timer (in milliseconds), row counter, CSV result export, and detailed syntax/table validation.\n\n5. **Live Data Explorer & Relational Schema Browser**\n   - Realistic sample records matching the report (`Hira Raza`, `Usman Yousaf`, `Samsung S24 Ultra`, `iPhone 15 Pro Max`, `HP Victus 15`, `Leopard`, `BlueEx`, `TCS`, etc.).\n   - Full SQL `CREATE TABLE` DDL generator with one-click clipboard copying.\n\n6. **Presentation Viva Mode & Global Search**\n   - **Presentation Mode**: Fullscreen, keyboard-navigable (`\342\206\220` / `\342\206\222` / `Space`) 9-slide defense deck structured for academic evaluation.\n   - **Global Search (`\342\214\230K` / `Ctrl+K`)**: Rapidly searches and cross-references entities, individual table attributes (e.g., typing `CustomerID` lists all parent and child tables), and relationship rules."
